1
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:05,620
There's a conversation we have to finish.

2
00:00:05,620 --> 00:00:08,170
What was it about?

3
00:00:08,170 --> 00:00:09,990
It was about caring.

4
00:00:09,990 --> 00:00:12,690
Oh?

5
00:00:12,690 --> 00:00:14,970
Yes, caring.

6
00:00:14,970 --> 00:00:16,830
I said that it makes me feel good

7
00:00:16,830 --> 00:00:19,000
that you care about Michelle.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,060
Well, I do care about Michelle.

9
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:25,000
And it makes me feel good that you care about me.

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,990
You know I do.

11
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:32,710
You're a ... wonderful friend.

12
00:00:32,710 --> 00:00:34,190
And it makes me feel good

13
00:00:34,190 --> 00:00:38,520
that you care about us.

14
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:41,190
Well ... well,

15
00:00:41,190 --> 00:00:42,210
I do, Harry.

16
00:00:42,210 --> 00:00:45,530
It's only natural that if I care about Michelle

17
00:00:45,530 --> 00:00:48,130
and I care about you,

18
00:00:48,130 --> 00:00:50,790
then I care about us.

19
00:00:50,790 --> 00:00:51,860
It's OK, Susan.

20
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:53,170
We had this part of the conversation

21
00:00:53,170 --> 00:00:54,230
before Michelle and her friends arrived.

22
00:00:54,230 --> 00:00:57,580
Now comes the good part.

23
00:00:57,580 --> 00:00:58,650
Like what?

24
00:00:58,650 --> 00:01:01,860
Well, assume that if you care about Michelle

25
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:03,020
and you care about me

26
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:05,580
and you care about us,

27
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:08,030
that we can talk about us.

28
00:01:08,030 --> 00:01:11,790
I mean--you and me.

29
00:01:11,790 --> 00:01:14,950
Isn't that right?

30
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:20,660
What are you trying to say, Harry?

31
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:24,530
What I'm trying to say ...

32
00:01:24,530 --> 00:01:29,900
since this is so easy ....

33
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:54,280
Here are ten letters that express my feelings for you.

34
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:56,500
Don't be silly, Harry.

35
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:57,740
You want a hint?

36
00:01:57,740 --> 00:01:59,040
It's two words.

37
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:02,410
You're making the game harder.

38
00:02:02,410 --> 00:02:04,370
Can't you figure it out?

39
00:02:04,370 --> 00:02:06,260
Seven letters ... two words ...

40
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:09,750
that express the feelings that I feel for you in my heart.

41
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:30,030
Harry, I get it! Harry

42
00:02:30,030 --> 00:02:33,700
Well? Does that mean you'll marry me?

43
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:43,070
Is that a proposal, or are we just playing a game?

44
00:02:43,070 --> 00:02:48,380
Sit down, Susan.

45
00:02:48,380 --> 00:03:05,170
There's something I have to ask you.

46
00:03:05,170 --> 00:03:09,990
Susan, will you marry me?

47
00:03:09,990 --> 00:03:12,170
It's such an important decision.

48
00:03:12,170 --> 00:03:15,320
There's so many things to talk about.

49
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:19,180
There are three things that have to be done first, Harry.

50
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:20,700
Three things?

51
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:24,170
First, we have to decide where to live.

52
00:03:24,170 --> 00:03:25,320
Well, that's easy.

53
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:26,400
We talked about that earlier.

54
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:27,330
We'll live in New York.

55
00:03:27,330 --> 00:03:29,440
All right.

56
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,280
Second,

57
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:34,140
we have to talk to Michelle together about being married.

58
00:03:34,140 --> 00:03:36,380
We'll do that immediately.

59
00:03:36,380 --> 00:03:38,340
What's the third thing?

60
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:40,590
You have to ask for my father's permission.

61
00:03:40,590 --> 00:03:42,770
Absolutely!

62
00:03:42,770 --> 00:03:44,130
But first things first.

63
00:03:44,130 --> 00:03:47,520
We have to go pick up Michelle.

64
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:52,100
Oh, I'm so happy, Harry!

65
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:55,100
Not as happy as I am.
